.TH CYPACHE\-APPS 7 2026-10-30 Cypache "Cypache Manual"
.ds AD l
.nh
.SH NAME
cypache\-apps \- the Python handlers, apps and views of Cypache sites
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
# controllers/news.py: answers GET /news, and /news/anything
import cypache

def get(request):
  return {"path": request.path, "page": request.args.get("page", "1")}

def post(request):
  request.setCookie("seen", "1")
  return cypache.redirect("/news")
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
A site's Python runs in Cypache's worker processes, as functions that take a
.B Request
and return the response.
A Site reaches them by exact path, through
.BR Site(routes=...) ,
or by file, through the apps and views directories
.RB ( Site(apps=...,\ views=...) ),
much as a PHP router does.
.BR cypache\-config (5)
describes the Site and the server.
.SH HANDLERS
A handler returns one of:
.TP
.B str
HTML
.RB ( "text/html; charset=utf\-8" ).
.TP
.B bytes
.BR application/octet\-stream .
.TP
.BR dict ", " list
JSON.
.TP
.B Response(body=b"", status=200, headers=(), contentType=None)
Anything else.
.B headers
is a dict, or a list of pairs for repeated headers such as
.BR Set\-Cookie .
Names the server controls
.RB ( Content\-Length ,
.BR Transfer\-Encoding ,
.BR Connection ,
.BR Date ,
\&...) and values with control characters raise
.B ValueError
when the
.B Response
is built.
Spaces and tabs around a value are dropped.
.PP
.B cypache.redirect(location, status=303)
makes a redirect (301, 302, 303, 307 or 308); characters a URL can't hold, non\-ASCII and backslashes among them, are percent\-encoded.
.PP
An exception in a handler, or an invalid return value, gives the client a plain
.B 500
and prints the traceback to stderr, the journal under systemd (at most 10 per 10 seconds per worker).
Raising
.B cypache.BadRequest
gives
.B 400
without a log line.
Only
.B SystemExit
and
.B KeyboardInterrupt
stop the worker.
.SH REQUEST
From the request:
.TP
.BR method ", " path ", " query ", " host ", " version ", " scheme
.B path
is percent\-decoded, with dot segments resolved and slashes merged;
.B query
is raw;
.B host
is lowercase, without the port;
.B scheme
is
.B \(dqhttps\(dq
or
.BR \(dqhttp\(dq .
.TP
.B headers
A dict of lowercase names; repeated fields are joined with
.BR \(dq,\ \(dq ,
cookies with
.BR \(dq;\ \(dq .
.TP
.B remote
The peer's address.
.TP
.BR body ", " stream
The whole body as bytes, or a new read\-only file over it.
.B body
reads a spooled body into memory at its first use, where
.B stream
doesn't.
.TP
.BR args ", " form ", " cookies
The query's parameters, the fields of an urlencoded or multipart body, and the cookies, parsed at first use.
A repeated name keeps its last value, and a repeated cookie its first.
.B args
and
.B form
also have
.BI getlist( name )
for all of a name's values, in order, as for checkboxes sharing a name.
More than 1000 fields, or a malformed form, give
.BR 400 .
.TP
.BR files ", " uploads
A multipart body's files, by field name (the last one per name), or all of them, as
.B Upload
objects (see UPLOADS).
.PP
For the response, when a handler returns a bare body or nothing:
.TP
.BR status ", " contentType
Writable; they apply to a bare body.
.TP
.BI setHeader( name ", " value )
Adds a header.
.TP
.BI setCookie( name ", " value ", maxAge=None, path=\(dq/\(dq, domain=None, secure=None, httpOnly=True, sameSite=\(dqLax\(dq)"
Adds a
.BR Set\-Cookie ,
.B Secure
by default over HTTPS.
The value must be cookie\-octets; encode it first otherwise.
.PP
Headers and cookies set this way are also added to a
.B Response
the handler returns.
Other attributes
.RB ( "request.user = ...\&" )
are free for the handlers along one request to share; the ones above are read\-only, except
.B status
and
.BR contentType .
.SH APPS
.EX
controllers/            Site(apps=...)
  auto.py               auto(request): runs first, for every request
  index.py              get(request): what nothing deeper matches
  news.py               get(request): /news
  world/
    auto.py             auto(request): runs for /world/...
    character.py        get, post: /world/character/Bubble,
                        with request.params == ("Bubble",)
    map.png.py          get(request): /world/map.png
    _queries.py         shared code: from . import _queries
views/                  Site(views=...)
  header.py             render(request): returns "<html>..."
  news.py               render(request): the view mirroring news.py
.EE
.TP
The walk
The request's path is walked against the apps directory one segment at a time.
Every
.B auto.py
on the way runs its
.BR auto(request) ,
the top one first, whatever the method.
The deepest
.IB name .py
named like the next segment is the endpoint, or else the nearest
.B index.py
on the way.
.B request.params
holds the segments the walk didn't consume.
.TP
Methods
The endpoint's
.BR get ,
.BR post ,
.BR put ,
.BR delete ,
.B patch
or
.B options
handles the request, and HEAD uses
.BR get .
Only functions the module defines itself count, so an imported
.B get
is no handler, and a decorator must keep the function's identity with
.BR functools.wraps .
Other methods get
.B 405
(OPTIONS
.BR 204 ),
with
.B Allow
listing those it has, after the autos on the walk ran.
.TP
Ending a request
An
.B auto
or endpoint that returns something ends the request with it as the response, such as
.B cypache.redirect(\(dq/login\(dq)
from an
.B auto.py
that checks a session.
.TP
Views
When nothing returns a response, the views render.
.BI request.view( path ", slot=\(dqbody\(dq)"
queues one into the
.BR header ,
.B body
or
.B footer
slot; the path is absolute from the views directory, or relative to the running handler's directory, and
.I name
finds
.IB name .py
or
.IB name /index.py\c
\&.
An endpoint that queues no body view, and dispatches nothing, gets the view mirroring its own path.
Each view's
.B render(request)
returns a
.BR str ,
and the slots render in order.
With
.B request.status
204, 205 or 304, no views render.
.TP
.BI request.dispatch( path )
Walks another path in the same request, after what's queued, skipping the
.B auto.py
files that already ran.
One request runs at most 64 handlers, so a dispatch loop ends in a
.BR 500 .
.TP
.B request.stop()
Cancels the endpoint of the walk the running
.B auto
belongs to, so an
.B auto.py
can take over the routing.
.TP
Loading
Modules are imported as a package per Site, so relative imports work, and directories are packages without running an
.IR __init__.py .
Names starting with
.B .\&
or
.B _
aren't routed, so helpers get
.B _
names: a
.I cache.py
that defines
.B get(key)
would be routed.
A routed module must define a method function
.RB ( auto
for
.IR auto.py ,
.B render
for a view).
Symlinks are refused, as is a
.IB name .py
next to a
.IB name /
directory.
.TP
Static files first
A file under the Site's static root is served without any
.B auto.py
running, so everything there is public.
.SH THREADS
.IP \(bu 2
Handlers run in a pool of threads in each worker
.RB ( serve(threads=16) ),
so one waiting on a database doesn't hold up the worker's other connections.
They run concurrently: module\-level state, such as a cache dict or a shared database connection, is shared between requests, so use thread\-safe objects or locks, or a connection per thread.
.IP \(bu 2
A handler, or a view's
.BR render ,
that never blocks can be marked
.B @cypache.inline
to run on the worker's event loop instead, which is faster.
An apps walk starts on the loop if its first handler is marked, and moves to the pool at the first handler or view that isn't.
.IP \(bu 2
With 16 jobs per thread already waiting, a request gets
.BR 503 .
A job doesn't run if its connection is gone when its turn comes.
.IP \(bu 2
A thread can't be stopped from outside, so a handler that hangs keeps its thread.
Past
.B handlerTimeout
(120 seconds) the worker prints where it's stuck, once.
When all of a worker's threads are stuck, it shuts down, and fastepoll starts a fresh one (with
.BR workers=1 ,
the server exits).
.IP \(bu 2
A process forked in a handler must end with
.BR os._exit() ;
one that returns into the server is ended with a message.
.IP \(bu 2
Over HTTPS, a client that half\-closes its connection while its handler runs gets no response, since TLS has no half\-close; the access log shows
.BR 499 .
.SH UPLOADS
A site that takes uploads raises
.B maxBodyBytes
in its
.BR serve() .
A body over
.B spoolBytes
(1 MiB) is written to an unnamed spool file while it arrives, so
.B request.body
would read it all into memory; read
.B request.stream
or the uploads instead.
An urlencoded
.B form
is parsed in memory, and limited to 1 MiB.
.PP
An
.B Upload
has:
.TP
.BR name ", " contentType ", " size
The form field's name, and the file's type and size.
.TP
.B filename
The client's name for the file, without directories, control or bidi characters.
Never use it as a path on the server.
.TP
.BR read() ", " open()
The file's bytes, or a read\-only file object over them.
.TP
.BI save( path ", mode=0o640)"
Writes the file to
.IR path ,
which must not exist yet: nothing there is overwritten or followed, a symlink included.
It's written unnamed and then linked into place, so it appears whole or not at all, and a spooled file is copied in the kernel.
It refuses a path among the code, where the file would run: in any Site's apps or views, in the directory of other code the server loaded, or in a directory on Python's import path.
Keep the directory outside the static root too, where an uploaded
.I .html
would be served as the site's own.
Under the service's unit it belongs to
.B cypache
with mode 750 and is listed in
.B ReadWritePaths=
(see
.BR cypache (8));
elsewhere
.B save()
fails with
.BR EROFS .
.PP
The multipart parser is strict: anything a parser in front, such as a firewall, could read differently gets
.BR 400 .
The body must start with its boundary, which may appear only as a delimiter line of its own;
parameters follow RFC 9110 strictly;
each part has one
.B form\-data
disposition with a UTF\-8 name;
and there are at most 1000 parts, with 16 KiB of header fields each, and 1 MiB of part headers and plain fields together.
Some clients' uploads get
.B 400
because of this: a filename ending in a backslash, a
.B \(dq
sent as
.B \e\(dq
(Go's
.BR mime/multipart ,
aiohttp), or a non\-ASCII filename from .NET.
.PP
A body must keep arriving at
.B minBodyRate
(8 KiB/s) on average, or it gets
.BR 408 ;
see
.BR cypache\-config (5).
.SH RELOAD
With
.B serve(reload=True)
(the default), a changed or new
.B .py
is served a second or so after it's saved: a new generation of the server loads all the code while the previous one serves.
Module\-level state starts afresh in each generation.
Code that doesn't load is reported, and the previous code keeps serving.
.SH EXAMPLES
An
.B auto.py
that keeps
.I /admin
and everything below it for signed\-in users:
.PP
.EX
# controllers/admin/auto.py; controllers/_session.py defines user()
import cypache
from .._session import user

def auto(request):
  request.user = user(request.cookies.get("__Host\-session"))
  if request.user is None:
    return cypache.redirect("/login")
.EE
.PP
An endpoint that saves an upload under a name of its own, and renders its view:
.PP
.EX
import secrets
import cypache

def post(request):
  photo = request.files.get("photo")
  if photo is None:
    raise cypache.BadRequest("no photo")
  photo.save(f"/srv/uploads/{secrets.token_hex(16)}")
  request.view("header", "header")
.EE
